{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":484497,"name":"Panda","username":"grokpanda","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/53a042/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T11:26:11.046Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEquipment: Macbook Air M1\u003cbr\u003e\nMacOS version: Tahoe 26.5\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot Info:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.43.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday, Sep 6, my Grok Bot lost connection to the computer. I tried all retries, updates and resets. See results below.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry connecting:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reconnecting…” for about a minute.\u003cbr\u003e\nThen, “Couldn’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe. If it doesn’t reconnect on its own, recover Grok Bot’s computer to keep the data.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Update failed. The update couldn’t finish. Agent Computer is still on its previous image. Your files and logins are kept; installed apps and packages are not. Any agent turn that cannot pause is discarded”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRecover my computer:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recover failed. The recovery couldn’t finish, so Grok Bot’s computer may still be unreachable. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry Recovery:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Recover failed. The recovery couldn’t finish, so Grok Bot’s computer may still be unreachable. Your Bots, files, and logins are safe.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReset:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state – retry to run the reset again.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRetry reset:\u003cbr\u003e\n“Reset failed. The reset couldn’t finish. Grok Bot’s computer may be in a partial state – retry to run the reset again.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso tried resetting via smartphone app, but no success.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFollow the steps described above.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProvided above\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-484497-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-484497-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-06T11:26:19.365Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":21,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":106.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Panda","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136423,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":true,"can_vote":false},{"id":484517,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-06T11:54:40.739Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Good news: your Grok Bot computer and Bots are fine, they’re working on our side and nothing is lost. You don’t need Reset, Recover, or Update here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a known issue on 0.43.0: if your Cursor password was recently changed or reset, or you signed out on another device, it signs out all devices. The 0.43.0 desktop app keeps the old session and, instead of asking you to sign in again, shows Couldn’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer. For the same reason, Update, Recover, and Reset fail too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFix: just sign out and sign back in in the desktop app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Grok Bot on Mac, click your name or avatar at the bottom left of the sidebar.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoose Sign out and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign in again with the same Cursor account you used to create your Bots, using your new password. If you have multiple Cursor accounts, make sure you pick the right one.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait about a minute. Your Bots should load.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you don’t see Sign out in the menu, right-click the Grok Bot icon in the menu bar, choose Quit, reopen the app, and try again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if it still won’t connect after signing in again.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-06T11:54:40.739Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":1.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":170775,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-lost-connection-with-its-computer-and-cant-update-recover-reset/170775/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":true,"topic_accepted_answer":true}],"stream":[484497,484517]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot lost connection with its computer and can\u0026rsquo;t update/recover/reset","id":170775,"title":"Grok Bot lost connection with its computer and can't update/recover/reset","posts